  "notes": "USAGE:\n{属|ぞく}する is a formal verb meaning to belong to a group, organization, or classification. It takes the particle に to mark the group one belongs to. In everyday speech, the more casual expressions ～に{入|はい}っている or ～の{一員|いちいん}だ are often preferred.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～に{属|ぞく}する: to belong to ~\n- ～に{属|ぞく}している: to be belonging to ~ (current state)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {組織|そしき}に{属|ぞく}する: to belong to an organization\n- {部門|ぶもん}に{属|ぞく}する: to belong to a department\n- {分類|ぶんるい}に{属|ぞく}する: to belong to a classification",
